// A `string_eq` inside a `make` body used to compile to an unpatched call,
// so it printed the two operand lengths instead of 1 or 0. The comparison
// routine is placed after the main program but the bodies are emitted after
// it, and the call sites are patched when the routine is placed, so a body
// comparison cannot be linked yet: it is refused rather than miscompiled.
make same(x: str) -> num {
  when string_eq(x, "a") == 1 {
    give 1
  }
  give 0
}
hold a = "a"
show same(a)
